# Proposed features recognized from through_chamfer.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.
# imported with --up z- (model z- is machine +Z) -- coordinates are post-rotation

# F1: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F1_Top Plane(z=0.0)

# F3: outer profile under top cap F1: vertical wall loop F3 F4 F6 F5, top at z=0.0, base at z=-12.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F3_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
feature F3_Profile ProfileBoss(z=0.0, extent=12.0
    0.0 -40.0
    0.0 0.0
    60.0 0.0
    60.0 -40.0
)

# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole; mouth bevel F2 absorbed, 1.0 deep at 90.0deg included -- extent runs to the virtual sharp corner (12.0) (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F7_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=11.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Hole, stepover=...)
# the mouth's 1.0mm bevel is the bore's chamfer_depth, at the included angle the
# model measures; a print that says otherwise is typed here (the three chamfer words are
# pick-two) -- break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F7_Hole)
feature F7_Hole CylinderBore(dia=12.0, extent=12.0, x=20.0, y=-20.0, chamfer_depth=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0)
